🧪 Software Optimization
If hardware upgrades aren’t an option, squeeze more out of what you’ve got:

Close background apps: Use Task Manager to kill memory hogs.

Use lightweight IDEs: Switch from PyCharm to Thonny or Geany.

Virtual memory boost: Increase your swap file size in system settings.

Disable startup programs: Speeds up boot and frees RAM.

